      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Try a fresh job at two in the afternoon. H seven went out at eleven and was readable two minutes later. H eight went out at one fifty. The broker received it at one fifty-five. The store published it at two oh three. Which heartbeat and what age belong in the two o’clock row?",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 18.224999999999998,
          "duration": 17.825,
          "until": 20.825
        },
        {
          "say": "H seven, three hours. H eight had reached the broker by two, but its publication mark is past the request line. Seal that first row. Move the request ten minutes forward. Now the scheduler reads H eight and reports a heartbeat age of twenty minutes.",
          "start": 20.825,
          "end": 37.655,
          "duration": 16.83,
          "until": 38.205
        },
        {
          "say": "Follow H eight from the worker to the store. Which timestamp did the scheduler subtract from two ten to get those twenty minutes?",
          "start": 38.205,
          "end": 45.775,
          "duration": 7.57,
          "until": 47.675
        },
        {
          "say": "Start at one fifty, when the worker sent it. At two ten, H eight is twenty minutes old. A later correction to its phase can keep that same worker timestamp. Neither publication nor correction rewrites the first receipt.",
          "start": 47.675,
          "end": 61.959999999999994,
          "duration": 14.285,
          "until": 62.459999999999994
        },
        {
          "say": "Now decide how to score the two-ten request. The row was written one minute ago. Across all required inputs the pipeline can vouch for events only through one forty. One heartbeat can arrive ahead of that frontier. Given that coverage, which scoring mode should this request record?",
          "start": 62.459999999999994,
          "end": 80.41499999999999,
          "duration": 17.955,
          "until": 82.565
        },
        {
          "say": "Use source coverage. From one forty to two ten, the pipeline lag is thirty minutes. Use the validated fallback and log degraded mode. The worker’s twenty minutes of silence answers a different question.",
          "start": 82.565,
          "end": 96.35,
          "duration": 13.785,
          "until": 97.1
        },
        {
          "say": "Replay that decision with one change. Suppose all inputs were covered through one fifty-five. Same worker timestamp, same row write, same request. Which mode does the scheduler record?",
          "start": 97.1,
          "end": 109.285,
          "duration": 12.185,
          "until": 111.785
        },
        {
          "say": "Fifteen minutes of lag. Score normally. This service includes fifteen minutes in the normal range. The heartbeat is still twenty minutes old, and the two o’clock row still says three hours. Carry those decision-time rows into the boosted-tree experiment and compare its alerts with a cheap baseline at the same operating cost.",
          "start": 111.785,
          "end": 132.415,
          "duration": 20.63,
          "until": 133.365
        }
      ],
